<a id="audio"></a>
<h2>3. Capture and recognition</h2>
<p>Capture timings derive from sample counts at 16 kHz, so UI scheduling delays do not affect silence detection.</p>
<p>For a block of N signed 16-bit samples, RMS is the square root of the mean squared normalized amplitude. The default threshold is 0.01. Accumulate 300 ms of above-threshold samples to arm automatic stop. Once armed, stop after the configured uninterrupted quiet interval (2 seconds by default). Counting samples avoids treating delayed callbacks as silence. The maximum take is 120 seconds, or 1,920,000 floats at 16 kHz. The full-take buffer costs about 7.7 MB before queued audio and inference memory.</p>
<p>Model inference proceeds independently of capture. Slow inference can delay visible hypotheses while the microphone still captures every block. A manual stop flushes any backlog and the trailing phrase. Settings test mode measures the same signal path and skips inference.</p>
@
<h3>AudioCapture.kt</h3>
<p>Read mono PCM16 from VOICE_RECOGNITION, normalize to floats and compute RMS for each 512-sample read. Keep at most 120 seconds. Test mode uses the same microphone path and omits the recording buffer.</p>
